Third-party software in Troupe's Ollama image (ollama/Dockerfile)

The image runs the `ollama` program and its CPU libraries, copied unmodified
from the official ollama/ollama image (the version is pinned in
ollama/Dockerfile), on Ubuntu 24.04.

- Ollama: MIT License, /usr/share/doc/ollama/LICENSE (from
  https://github.com/ollama/ollama at the pinned tag).
- llama.cpp and ggml (the libggml-* and libllama* libraries): MIT License,
  /usr/lib/ollama/LLAMA_CPP_LICENSE; the code llama.cpp vendors:
  /usr/lib/ollama/LLAMA_CPP_VENDORS_LICENSE.
- cpp-httplib: MIT License, /usr/lib/ollama/CPP_HTTPLIB_LICENSE.
- The Go runtime and standard library, compiled into `ollama`: BSD 3-Clause
  License, /usr/lib/ollama/GO_LICENSE.
- GNU OpenMP runtime (/usr/lib/ollama/libgomp.so.1), part of GCC: GNU General
  Public License version 3 with the GCC Runtime Library Exception 3.1. The
  license texts are in /usr/share/doc/gcc-14-base/copyright (and
  /usr/share/common-licenses/GPL-3); the source is available from
  https://gcc.gnu.org and Ubuntu's gcc packages
  (https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/gcc-14).
- LLVM OpenMP runtime (/usr/lib/ollama/libomp.so), part of the LLVM project:
  Apache License 2.0 with LLVM Exceptions (parts also under the University of
  Illinois/NCSA and MIT licenses), https://llvm.org/LICENSE.txt; source from
  https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project (openmp/).
- Ubuntu 24.04 packages keep their own licenses, in /usr/share/doc/*/copyright.
